menu "Walter Sensor Node Board Selection"

    choice BOARD_VARIANT
        prompt "Target board"
        default BOARD_VARIANT_WALTER_FEELS
        help
            Which physical board board_pins.h's GPIO assignments should
            match. This is independent of the chip target (set via
            `idf.py set-target`) - for the DevKit test rig you need
            both `idf.py set-target esp32` AND this option set to
            "Generic ESP32 DevKit".

        config BOARD_VARIANT_WALTER_FEELS
            bool "Walter + Walter Feels carrier board (production)"
            help
                SDI-12, I2C, and SD card pins as wired on the Walter
                Feels carrier board. Requires the esp32s3 chip target.

        config BOARD_VARIANT_ESP32_DEVKIT_TEST
            bool "Generic ESP32 DevKit V1 (I2C-only test rig)"
            help
                For testing the firmware without a Walter/Walter Feels
                board in hand: a plain ESP32 DevKit V1 with I2C sensors
                only (e.g. ADS1115 ADCs) wired to the standard ESP32
                DevKit I2C pins (GPIO21/22). SDI-12, SD card, and
                cellular are all left unconfigured/disabled - those
                subsystems safely no-op without hardware. Requires the
                esp32 (classic) chip target.
    endchoice

endmenu
